### StreamPulse API collection (IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client compatible)
### All requests go through api-gateway on :8080 except where noted.
### Run "Register tenant" and "Login" first and copy the returned accessToken into
### the @accessToken variable below to exercise the authenticated requests.

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@accessToken = REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN
@refreshToken = REPLACE_WITH_REFRESH_TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN
@ruleId = REPLACE_WITH_RULE_ID


### ============================== auth-service ==============================

### Register a new tenant + its first ADMIN user
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/register-tenant
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantName": "Acme Corp",
  "tenantSlug": "acme",
  "adminEmail": "admin@acme.io",
  "adminPassword": "SuperSecret123"
}

### Login
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@acme.io",
  "password": "SuperSecret123",
  "tenantSlug": "acme"
}

### Refresh (rotates the refresh token; the old one becomes unusable)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}


### =========================== ingestion-service =============================

### Ingest a CPU usage event (requires ADMIN or MEMBER role)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "source": "web-01",
  "type": "CPU_USAGE",
  "metricName": "cpu.usage.percent",
  "value": 97.4,
  "attributes": {
    "region": "us-east-1"
  }
}

### Ingest an error-rate event that should breach a rule
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "source": "checkout-service",
  "type": "ERROR_RATE",
  "metricName": "error.rate",
  "value": 12.5
}


### ========================= rules-engine-service ============================

### Create an alert rule (requires ADMIN)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/rules
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "name": "High CPU usage",
  "metricName": "cpu.usage.percent",
  "comparator": "GREATER_THAN",
  "threshold": 90.0,
  "severity": "CRITICAL",
  "enabled": true
}

### List all rules for the caller's tenant
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/rules
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get a single rule
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/rules/{{ruleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Update a rule (requires ADMIN)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/rules/{{ruleId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "name": "High CPU usage (revised)",
  "metricName": "cpu.usage.percent",
  "comparator": "GREATER_THAN",
  "threshold": 85.0,
  "severity": "CRITICAL",
  "enabled": true
}

### Delete a rule (requires ADMIN)
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/v1/rules/{{ruleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### ========================= notification-service ============================

### Paged notification history for the caller's tenant
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/notifications?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### SSE fallback stream (open in a browser or an SSE-aware client; curl -N also works)
GET {{gateway}}/sse/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### WebSocket (not expressible as a plain HTTP request):
### ws://localhost:8080/ws/notifications
### Connect with a WebSocket client and pass the same bearer token via the gateway,
### which forwards X-Tenant-Id/X-User-Id/X-User-Roles on the upgrade request.


### ============================== actuator / docs =============================

### Health check for any service, e.g. api-gateway itself
GET {{gateway}}/actuator/health

### OpenAPI docs (per service, direct port — not proxied through the gateway)
GET http://localhost:8081/v3/api-docs
###
GET http://localhost:8082/v3/api-docs
###
GET http://localhost:8083/v3/api-docs
###
GET http://localhost:8084/v3/api-docs
